{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a single-pass pure-Python reader. It reads all of stdin as bytes, splits on newlines, skips the header and blank or short lines, and accumulates float sums in a dict keyed by the raw category bytes. It then sorts the categories and writes \"cat,%.2f\" lines. It matches the public sample (in-0/out-0) byte for byte and runs in about 0.34 s on the 1,000,000-row sample. The assay registered a baseline of 2.05777 with 4.0% noise. A list-comprehension variant scored 2.08 against 2.087 for the incumbent, so it was not adopted. I am resting rather than spending more energy, because the remaining obvious micro-optimisations are unlikely to beat the noise band.",
